# CODEOWNERS — sensitivity map for Facet (NON-ENFORCING)
#
# NOTE: Facet uses full auto-merge with NO review gate, so this file does NOT
# block any merge. `require_code_owner_review` is off in the branch ruleset.
# It is kept as a map of sensitive paths and to auto-request @NickCrew as a
# courtesy reviewer (a ping, never a block) on PRs authored by someone other
# than the owner.
#
# Last matching pattern wins: default (everything) -> exempt -> protected (last).
# If a review gate is reintroduced later (e.g. a non-owner bot author plus
# code-owner review), this routing becomes live again exactly as written.

# ── Default: anything not matched below routes to review ─────────────────────
*                       @NickCrew

# ── Exempt: CI is sufficient (no owner = no required review) ─────────────────
/docs/
*.md
/tests/
/src/test/
/site/
/public/
/brand/

# ── (optional) trust CI + CodeQL + the claude-review bot for pure UI work ────
# Uncomment to keep frontend churn out of the review queue. Start tight; loosen
# only if the queue actually hurts.
# /src/components/
# /src/routes/
# /src/themes/
# /src/hooks/

# ── Protected: re-asserted LAST so they win over the exemptions above ────────
/proxy/                 @NickCrew   # trust boundary: auth, billing, AI, persistence, server
/supabase/              @NickCrew   # schema & migrations
/src/identity/          @NickCrew
/src/routes/identity/   @NickCrew
/src/routes/account/    @NickCrew
/src/routes/admin/      @NickCrew
/src/persistence/       @NickCrew
/src/engine/            @NickCrew   # core generation — tests miss quality regressions
/src/store/             @NickCrew   # subtle state bugs
/.github/               @NickCrew   # CI / release config / this file
/scripts/               @NickCrew
/Dockerfile             @NickCrew
/fly.toml               @NickCrew
/vercel.json            @NickCrew
/vite.config.ts         @NickCrew
/vite.build.config.ts   @NickCrew
/eslint.config.js       @NickCrew
tsconfig*.json          @NickCrew
/package.json           @NickCrew
/pnpm-lock.yaml         @NickCrew
/pnpm-workspace.yaml    @NickCrew
/.npmrc                 @NickCrew
.env.example            @NickCrew   # template changes shift runtime config
